      "writtenOn": "2021-04-24T13:14:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This bug may not apply to upstream as migrate_tasks() would be called from stop_machine with *all* CPUs in the tight busy loop with interrupts disabled. So there is not chance of some other CPU acquiring the rq::lock and clearing rq::clock_update_flags. However, CPU pause call migrate_tasks() with other CPUs not in stop machine loop, so there is possibility of taking rq::lock while it is dropped.\n\nThis code is not present in linus latest tree due to migration disable feature refactored this. So if we have to send it, this needs to be against 5.10 stable but it won\u0027t fix any real issue in the upstream...\n\nDo you still want us to submit this fix to upstream?\n\nThanks,\nPavan",
      "parentUuid": "5c5adf81_9c9d06af",
      "revId": "2bf87fd80aa53761ba81425766aff73a6d59e891",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
